  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) achieves only 20.8%, indicating RNA is the dominant modality and the key design decisions lie on the RNA side. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether multiprofile (multiple profiles per cell with aggregation) improves over singleprofile for RNA. Question: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) directly extends config_001 by adding multiprofile with simple average-pool aggregation, isolating the effect of profile setting while keeping the encoder identical. This is the best next experiment because it is the minimal, cleanest change from our strongest baseline, resolves whether multiprofile is worth pursuing (which gates many downstream experiments on aggregation and encoder choice), and avoids jumping to multimodal fusion or a new encoder before establishing whether the profile axis matters."
}

